1. Derived cryptography: Luigi Auriemma, through GameSpy-Openspy-Core
------------------------------------------------------------------
FruitSpy's server/fruitspy/crypto.py is a Python adaptation of Luigi Auriemma's
GameSpy cryptography implementations as included in:

  devzspy/GameSpy-Openspy-Core
  https://github.com/devzspy/GameSpy-Openspy-Core
  Reviewed source revision: 15ba5afe346447f95c1b097a45826b018cfe4a76
  https://github.com/devzspy/GameSpy-Openspy-Core/tree/15ba5afe346447f95c1b097a45826b018cfe4a76

The specific source-to-adaptation mapping is:

  common/gsmsalg.cpp — GSMSALG 0.3.3
  Copyright 2004,2005,2006,2007,2008 Luigi Auriemma
  FruitSpy adaptation: gsseckey(), QR challenge-response generation.

  common/gs_peerchat.cpp and common/gs_peerchat.h
  GS peerchat encryption/decryption algorithm 0.2
  Copyright 2004,2005,2006 Luigi Auriemma
  FruitSpy adaptation: PeerChatCipher, including the fixed-six-byte game-key
  behavior in the OpenSpy variant.

  common/enctypex_decoder.cpp — GS enctypeX servers list decoder/encoder 0.1.3a
  Copyright 2008,2009 Luigi Auriemma
  FruitSpy adaptation: EnctypeX initialization, encryption, and decryption.

